DECISION: RECORD, DO NOT DERIVE
Div 40 needs per-asset effective lives, a prime cost / diminishing value
election, and the second-hand plant restriction. A QS determines these.
Deriving them here would duplicate paid work and take on liability that
conflicts with conductor/product.md. The panel captures their stated
annual figures and keeps the schedule as evidence.

WHY THE COMPARISON LINE MATTERS
The Div 43 register computed from the owner's own capital works is shown
next to the QS figure, with a note that the surveyor's number is normally
HIGHER because it covers original construction the owner never paid for.
Without that note the two would read as a discrepancy and invite someone
to "correct" the larger, correct figure downward.

ABSENCE IS STATED, NOT SILENT
With no schedule recorded the panel says plant and equipment is not
tracked and why, so the pack can instruct the accountant to request it.
An omitted deduction that nobody is told about is the failure mode here.

Storage path preservation: saving figures without re-uploading keeps the
existing report rather than clearing storage_path, so editing a number
does not orphan the evidence.

